Thread the new 7th argument through `deja::replay` and clear the lints that
were blocking the stable/MSRV/V2 CI jobs, plus land the pending migration-URL
wiring and the KYC/KYB verification core.

CI fixes
- external_services: pass the new `MissPolicy` argument to `deja::replay`
  (`FailStop` at the absent-transport boundary, `Absorb` at the Superposition
  boundary) — fixes E0061 in both call paths.
- storage_impl: `ConnectionSetup::is_needed` takes `self` by value
  (`clippy::trivially_copy_pass_by_ref`).
- common_utils: drop the trailing semicolon from the `type_name!` macro
  (`semicolon_in_expressions_from_non_local_macros`); the E0061 abort had been
  masking this lint.
- hyperswitch_connectors: `cargo +nightly fmt` over `korapay.rs` and
  `korapay/transformers.rs` (formatting job).

Migrations
- Add `MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL` (session-mode/direct, unsafe through a
  transaction-mode pooler) with fallback to `DATABASE_URL`: new
  `migration_database_url` in the justfile used by run_migration/migrate/
  migrate_v2/migrate_v2_compatible; forwarded by both compose files; preferred
  by the migration-runner entrypoint.

KYC/KYB (greenfield core, not yet wired to suspension/Novu)
- common_types: new `merchant_verification` module — verification tiers, the
  general amount threshold, and the one-year unregistered-business grace
  period, as a pure decision core with unit tests.

HANDOVER.md: record the 2026-10-09 session (real five-job failure set and fixes).

Co-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>
